            <ArticleTitle>Angina pectoris in consequence of subtotal subclavian artery stenosis 2 years after CABG.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0029-1186239</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of an 80-year-old male patient who complained of recurrent angina 2 years after coronary bypass grafting using a left mammary artery (LIMA). This was caused by a new subtotal subclavian artery stenosis before the origin of the LIMA. The left subclavian artery was stented and the patient experienced complete relief.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
